ers Princewill Umanmielen and Devin Harper, who signed revenue sharing contracts to return to the Rebels this season before joining former coach Lane Kiffin at LSU.","published":"2026-07-29T12:13:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49475144/ole-miss-sues-former-players-princewill-umanmielen-devin-harper-now-lsu-breach-contract","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Arkansas State tells Butch Jones he's out at end of year","description":"Arkansas State has informed football coach Butch Jones that he's out at the end of the year, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Monday night.","published":"2026-11-17T02:24:24.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50506952/sources-butch-jones-arkansas-state-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-16T23:15:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Illinois may turn to third-string QB Boyd after Houser injury","description":"Illinois might turn to third-string quarterback Carson Boyd this week against No. 15 Iowa after starter Katin Houser suffered a broken nose Friday at UCLA that required surgery.","published":"2026-11-16T21:42:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504718/illinois-turn-third-string-qb-boyd-houser-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rivers says NC State only college job he would have taken","description":"New coach Philip Rivers said NC State was the only college job he would have taken.","published":"2026-11-16T22:20:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504530/rivers-says-nc-state-only-college-job-taken","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest up to No. 10 in AP poll as top teams avoid upsets","description":"Wake Forest's move up to No. 10 was the only week-over-week change atop the AP poll as the top nine teams remained unchanged.","published":"2026-11-16T20:48:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504044/wake-forest-no-10-ap-poll-top-teams-avoid-upsets","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas' Manning to participate in senior day, mum on future","description":"Texas quarterback Arch Manning said Monday he will participate in Saturday's senior day ceremonies despite having one year of eligibility remaining.","published":"2026-11-16T20:31:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503997/texas-arch-manning-participate-senior-day","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wisconsin safety Matt Jung to have season-ending ankle surgery","description":"Wisconsin safety Matt Jung will undergo season-ending ankle surgery, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-16T21:10:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503973/wisconsin-safety-matt-jung-season-ending-ankle-surgery","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas DL Hero Kanu undergoes season-ending surgery on arm","description":"Texas starting defensive tackle Hero Kanu had season-ending surgery on his arm Monday, coach Steve Sarkisian announced.","published":"2026-11-16T20:55:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503942/texas-dl-hero-kanu-undergoes-season-ending-surgery-arm","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4917971/princewill-umanmielen","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princewill_Umanmielen"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Princewill Umanmielen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princewill_Umanmielen","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:37Z","intro":"Princewill Umanmielen (born February 13, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the LSU Tigers. He previously played for the Nebraska Cornhuskers and Ole Miss Rebels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Umanmielen attended Manor High School in Manor, Texas. In his final two seasons, he totaled 47 tackles for loss and 21 sacks. A four-star recruit, Umanmielen committed to play college football at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln over offers from Arkansas, Florida, and Washington."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"NEBRASKA\nAs a freshman, Umanmielen recorded 22 tackles, 4.5 tackles-for-loss, and a sack. As a result, he was named a second-team freshman All-American. The following season, he tallied 13 tackles and 2.5 tackles-for-loss, before entering the transfer portal.\n\nOLE MISS\nOn December 14, 2024, Umanmielen, a top-ranked transfer, announced his decision to transfer to the University of Mississippi to play for the Ole Miss Rebels."}],"family":[{"relation":"Sibling","name":"Princely Umanmielen","description":"American football defensive end (born 2002)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princely_Umanmielen"}]}}